  "notes": "0.1.686b: bounded screen-capture replies\n\nFIRECAP ASCII replies now use the bounded text-frame transport with queue drain and TX re-kick instead of fire-and-forget submission. Response fields, pixel hex bytes and CRCs are preserved; the USB firmware update payload format and BLE recovery policy are unchanged.\n\nThe screenshot tool retries the same idempotent END nonce at most three times. A CRC-valid saved image and an unconfirmed session cleanup are reported separately; unconfirmed cleanup returns failure instead of silent success. Partial image data is never saved as a successful capture, and the original read error remains primary.\n\nFocused host regressions, immutable source/build evidence, installed transaction evidence and public download hashes are recorded separately. This update does not claim complete physical/optical QA or a proven cause for every historical USB timeout.\n",
